        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): detect native bot mentions in group gating",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSignal groups can be configured with `requireMention=true` so side chatter stays quiet until the bot is explicitly mentioned. Signal native mentions arrive as structured `dataMessage.mentions[]` metadata plus object-replacement characters in the message text. The current Signal handler renders those placeholders as `@<uuid>` or `@<phone>`, then relies on text mention regexes. Selecting the bot from Signal's native mention UI can therefore fail to wake the bot unless a matching text fallback happens to be configured.\n\nThis also leaves `canDetectMention` tied only to configured text regexes and passes `hasAnyMention=false` even when Signal supplied structured mention metadata.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis patch keeps the fix inside the Signal plugin and adds a small native mention fact resolver. It compares structured Signal mention metadata against the current bot account identity:\n\n- UUID via `channels.signal.accountUuid`\n- phone number via the existing E.164 normalizer and `channels.signal.account`\n\nThe event handler now combines text fallback and native metadata:\n\n- `wasMentioned` is true for text fallback or a native mention that targets the current bot account.\n- `canDetectMention` reflects text regexes or available bot account identity.\n- `hasAnyMention` reflects valid structured Signal mention metadata so the shared mention-decision contract can distinguish command bypass from messages mentioning someone else.\n\nMentions of other participants do not trigger the bot. Missing bot identity does not become a false mention. Existing text fallback, group access checks, pending history, attachment restraint, control-command handling, direct messages, and `requireMention=false` behavior stay unchanged.\n\nThis supersedes #69413, which was closed without merge, by adding the missing capability facts, event-handler coverage, and docs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBefore:\n\n> A user could select the bot from Signal's native mention UI in a `requireMention` group and get no response because the rendered `@uuid`/`@phone` text did not match the configured agent-name regex.\n\nAfter:\n\n> Native Signal mentions targeting the current bot account pass mention gating. Mentions of other participants remain silent and are kept only as bounded pending context. A later bot mention can include recent skipped group context and reply in the same group.\n\nDocs now describe Signal native mention behavior, `accountUuid`, text mention fallback, and a mention-gated group configuration with bounded history.\n\n### Behavior Change\n\nSignal groups with `requireMention=true` that have a configured bot identity (`accountUuid`/`account`) but no text mention regexes previously fell through to pass-through handling. After this change they enforce mention gating via native Signal mention metadata. Group chatter that did not mention the bot but previously reached it may now be gated. This is intended and makes native-only `requireMention` groups behave as documented. Maintainers with such groups should expect stricter, correct gating after upgrade.\n\n### Trust Model\n\n`dataMessage.mentions[]` is sender-supplied. A group member could craft metadata naming the bot; the only effect is waking the bot, which any member can already do via a normal Signal mention. Native facts are still validated against a real object-replacement placeholder span, so malformed metadata does not become a bot mention.\n\n### Native Identity Note\n\nFor full native mention coverage, configure `channels.signal.accountUuid` alongside `channels.signal.account`. Phone-only identity can still match phone-backed mention metadata, but UUID-only Signal mention metadata requires `accountUuid`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Base: `4ecb45b chore: update default check gate expectations`\n- Head: `83ac15c979a4`\n- Static whitespace check: `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD`\n- Focused Signal mention-gating tests passed on this branch:\n  `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- Production TypeScript check passed:\n  `pnpm tsgo:prod`\n\nThe focused Signal suite covers:\n\n- native bot UUID mention without text mention patterns;\n- native bot phone mention with E.164 normalization;\n- native mention of another participant stays silent and records pending context;\n- malformed matching metadata does not become a bot mention;\n- no-detector behavior remains explicit;\n- helper facts for bot mention, unrelated mention, malformed span, and missing bot identity.\n\n### Redacted Live Signal Proof\n\nThis is the sanitized inspectable artifact from a live 3-person private Signal smoke. IDs, UUIDs, phone numbers, group IDs, raw message bodies, and private participant context are intentionally omitted.\n\n```text\nenvironment: live private Signal group\nruntime: OpenClaw gateway with this PR's Signal mention patch installed\nconfig.runtime: { signalConfigured: true, groupPolicy: \"allowlist\", groupAllowFromCount: 1, groupsCount: 1, requireMentionGroups: 1, accountUuidSet: true, historyLimit: 3 }\nconfig.template: { signalConfigured: true, groupPolicy: \"allowlist\", groupAllowFromCount: 1, groupsCount: 1, requireMentionGroups: 1, accountUuidSet: true, historyLimit: 3 }\nsignal.probe: { configured: true, running: true, probeOk: true, probeStatus: 200 }\nsession.markerScan: { proofMarker: \"96738\", markerFileCount: 11, rawContentPrinted: false }\n\ncase: native bot mention from Signal UI\ninput: Signal native mention picker selected the bot display name; no text mention regex fallback was used\nexpected PR facts: { canDetectMention: true, hasAnyMention: true, wasMentioned: true, shouldSkip: false }\nobserved: bot account replied in the same group with the controlled proof marker\n\ncase: native non-bot participant mention from Signal UI\ninput: Signal native mention picker selected another group participant, not the bot\ndelivery: Signal message info showed delivery to both the bot account and the mentioned participant\nexpected PR facts: { canDetectMention: true, hasAnyMention: true, wasMentioned: false, shouldSkip: true }\nobserved: no bot reply was produced after the quiet window\n```\n",
        "branch": "codex/signal-native-mention-gating",
